      "focusOrTheme": "Wrongful conviction, coerced false confessions, juvenile suspects, racial bias, media frenzy, DNA exoneration.",
      "summaryNotes": "Provides a detailed account of the wrongful conviction of five teenagers in the high-profile \"Central Park Jogger\" case. It highlights the intense pressure, coercive interrogation tactics, and racial undertones that led to false confessions and convictions despite a lack of physical evidence connecting them. Their exoneration came years later when the actual perpetrator confessed and DNA confirmed his guilt. The case became a symbol of systemic flaws in the justice system, particularly regarding treatment of minority youth and reliance on confessions.",
